From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:07:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 73/99] v8: e2k: WebAssembly: Liftoff, linkage, jump tables

d8 builds with v8_enable_webassembly = true and runs modules compiled by
TurboFan and by Liftoff.

- wasm-linkage.h, liftoff-assembler-defs.h: the registers of loong64 (the
  instruction layer is the same).
- liftoff-assembler-e2k-inl.h: the loong64 file. The frame set-up keeps
  its three instructions in their own slots and counts branch offsets in
  instructions; an i32 returned by a C function is sign-extended (clang
  returns it zero-extended).
- Jump tables are built by the instruction layer
  (Assembler::WasmJumpSlot, WasmFarJumpSlot, WasmLazyCompileSlot): a jump
  slot is one instruction, b, patched in its 32-bit displacement; a far
  jump slot is li64 and jirl, patched in the 64-bit literal; a lazy
  compile slot is li and b. A code space is at most 512 MB.
- e2k joins loong64 in the lists of architectures with the generic
  JS-to-wasm and wasm-to-JS wrappers, far jumps between code spaces, i64
  rotations in Liftoff, the JSPI handler table entry and code coverage.
- CpuFeatures::SupportsSimd128() is false: modules with simd128 are
  refused.

The trap handler stays off (explicit bounds and null checks).
